-- int-tests-licence-life.l4: whole scenarios S01 to S04, S09 to S11 and S16 of expectations.md: a licence from application to lapse,
-- revocation, suspension and extension, crossing groups 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7 and 8.  Every expected value was written in expectations.md
-- from the Hebrew text before this module was run; the provision that gives it is cited beside it.

§ `Tests: the life of a licence`

§§ `S01. Dana: application, grant, validity, lapse, unlicensed work, sanction (groups 2, 4, 8, 7, 1, 6)`

`dana: the applicant` MEANS `fixture: an applicant with no prior training, being` `fixture: Dana, an individual`
`dana: the application of 1 December 2025` MEANS `fixture: an application by` `dana: the applicant` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1)
`dana: the licence granted on 1 December 2025` MEANS `fixture: an ordinary licence held by` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `of kind` `grade 1 licence` `granted on` (YMD 2025 12 1)

-- The route: Second Schedule Part A item 1 ("no prior training or experience"): up to 350 hours conferring the grade 1 certificate, or the 3-unit certificate.
`dana: the items of the Second Schedule` MEANS `int — the training the Second Schedule requires for` `dana: the application of 1 December 2025`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 1 AND item's `the part: the licence kind it leads to` EQUALS `grade 1 licence`) `dana: the items of the Second Schedule`
#ASSERT NOT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the part: the licence kind it leads to` EQUALS `grade 2 licence`) `dana: the items of the Second Schedule`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 1 AND (`Second Schedule — the ceiling on the hours of` (at (item's `column B: any one of`) 0)) EQUALS 350) `dana: the items of the Second Schedule`

-- The grant: s.6(a)(1) to (4) hold, the programme has the Registrar's consent, 284 paid is the fee of regulation 2(c) as made (no update before 1.1.2026), after the commencement day.
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` `dana: the application of 1 December 2025` `with the programme being` (JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar consented to`) `and the amount paid being` 284)
-- 283 is not "in full": regulation 4 bars the Registrar.
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` `dana: the application of 1 December 2025` `with the programme being` (JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar consented to`) `and the amount paid being` 283)
-- More than the fee is paid in full (group 8, fork F14).
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` `dana: the application of 1 December 2025` `with the programme being` (JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar consented to`) `and the amount paid being` 400)
-- A programme without the Registrar's consent (s.19(b)): the training was not completed in an approved programme.
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` `dana: the application of 1 December 2025` `with the programme being` (JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar did not consent to`) `and the amount paid being` 284)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` `dana: the application of 1 December 2025` `with the programme being` NOTHING `and the amount paid being` 284)
-- The alternative reading of "approved": a programme that needs no consent satisfies the requirement.  A programme that leads to a final certificate needs it.
#ASSERT `int (a programme that needs no consent satisfies the requirement) — the requirement of the Registrar's consent is met by the programme in` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` `dana: the application of 1 December 2025` `with the programme being` (JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar consented to`) `and the amount paid being` 284)
#ASSERT NOT `int (a programme that needs no consent satisfies the requirement) — the requirement of the Registrar's consent is met by the programme in` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` `dana: the application of 1 December 2025` `with the programme being` (JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar did not consent to`) `and the amount paid being` 284)
-- An application on 15.7.2025, the day before the commencement day: the sources do not say whether the Registrar's duty had begun.
`dana: the application of 15 July 2025` MEANS `fixture: an application by` `dana: the applicant` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2025 7 15)
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` `dana: the application of 15 July 2025` `with the programme being` (JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar consented to`) `and the amount paid being` 284) BECAUSE "the Law fixes a commencement only for work on a system (s.63(a)); it does not say when the Registrar's duty to grant (s.6) begins, and the day is before the commencement day of s.63(a)(1)"
-- Group 2's own ungated reading: every condition holds and no fee had yet been fixed, so regulation 4 bars nothing.
#ASSERT `int (with no commencement gate) — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant for a given programme on` `dana: the application of 15 July 2025` `with the programme being` (JUST `fixture: a programme the Registrar consented to`) `and the amount paid being` 0)

-- Validity: five years after 1.12.2025 is 1.12.2030; 31 March of the fifth year from the year of grant is 31.3.2030 (2025 + 5, group 2 fork FV1); the earlier governs.
#ASSERT `s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence` `dana: the licence granted on 1 December 2025` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence granted on 1 December 2025` (YMD 2025 12 1)
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence granted on 1 December 2025` (YMD 2030 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence granted on 1 December 2025` (YMD 2025 11 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence granted on 1 December 2025` (YMD 2030 4 1)

-- The work: 10 kW with R134a, commenced since 16.1.2027 (s.63(a)(2)); activity A.1(2) is listed under grade 1.
`dana: the work on 1 April 2030` MEANS `fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST `dana: the licence granted on 1 December 2025`) `on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `on the system` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`
`dana: the work on 31 March 2030` MEANS `fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST `dana: the licence granted on 1 December 2025`) `on` (YMD 2030 3 31) `on the system` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`
#ASSERT `int — the Law has commenced for work on the system on the day` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") (YMD 2030 4 1)
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` `dana: the work on 1 April 2030` EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the person may do the work of` `dana: the work on 1 April 2030`
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` `dana: the work on 31 March 2030` EQUALS `the work is permitted: the person holds a licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work, and works within its conditions`
#ASSERT `int — the person may do the work of` `dana: the work on 31 March 2030`
-- F8, the alternative: a licence that is not in force still counts as a licence held, so the work falls under item (2).
#ASSERT `int (a licence not in force counting as held) — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` `dana: the work on 1 April 2030` EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work`
-- The violation of the lapsed licensee: Third Schedule item (1).
`dana: the violation of 1 April 2030` MEANS `int — the violation committed under section 3(a) by` `dana: the work on 1 April 2030` `with the reference` "dana-2030-04-01"
#ASSERT `dana: the violation of 1 April 2030` EQUALS JUST (Violation WITH `the violator` IS `fixture: Dana, an individual`, `the listed violation` IS `work with no licence at all`, `reference for the act` IS "dana-2030-04-01", `date of the act` IS YMD 2030 4 1)
#ASSERT `int — the violation committed under section 3(a) by` `dana: the work on 31 March 2030` `with the reference` "dana-2030-03-31" EQUALS NOTHING

-- The sanction.  Previous violation: Dana, s.3(a) (item (2)), 10.1.2029, a sanction imposed; two years after 10.1.2029 is 10.1.2031, so 1.4.2030 is inside: a repeat violation.
`dana: the previous violation of 10 January 2029` MEANS `Previous violation` WITH
    `the violator` IS `fixture: Dana, an individual`
    `the listed violation` IS `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`
    `date of the act` IS YMD 2029 1 10
    `a financial sanction was imposed for it` IS TRUE
    `the violator was convicted for it` IS FALSE
`dana: the pricing without an earlier violation` MEANS `fixture: the pricing of a violation that did not continue and has no earlier violation, updated on` (YMD 2030 6 15)
`dana: the pricing with the earlier violation` MEANS `Facts for pricing a violation` WITH
    `the violation continued from` IS NOTHING
    `the last day the violation continued` IS YMD 2030 4 1
    `the previous violations of the violator` IS LIST `dana: the previous violation of 10 January 2029`
    `the day on which the amount is updated` IS YMD 2030 6 15
    `the year of the first update day` IS 2026
    `the index readings` IS `fixture: the index readings for the sanctions`
-- Chapter 6 commences with the later of 16.1.2027 and 1.6.2026 (the hypothetical regulation under s.46): in force on 1.4.2030.
#ASSERT `int — Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act, given the facts` (YMD 2030 4 1) `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46`
-- 20,000 (item (1)) times 102/100 = 20,400, plus an equal amount for the repeat violation: 40,800.
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for` `dana: the violation of 1 April 2030` `priced from` `dana: the pricing with the earlier violation` `with the commencement` `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` EQUALS `the sanction is` 40800
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for` `dana: the violation of 1 April 2030` `priced from` `dana: the pricing without an earlier violation` `with the commencement` `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` EQUALS `the sanction is` 20400
-- The same through the one-call form for a piece of work.
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for the work of` `dana: the work on 1 April 2030` `with the reference` "dana-2030-04-01" `priced from` `dana: the pricing with the earlier violation` `with the commencement` `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` EQUALS `the sanction is` 40800
-- Permitted work prices nothing.
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for the work of` `dana: the work on 31 March 2030` `with the reference` "dana-2030-03-31" `priced from` `dana: the pricing without an earlier violation` `with the commencement` `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` EQUALS `no listed violation: the facts breach no provision that the Third Schedule prices`
-- On the sources alone (no regulation under s.46 known), Chapter 6 on 1.4.2030 is not answered: a refusal, never "not yet" and never "yes".
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2030 4 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the sanction for` `dana: the violation of 1 April 2030` `priced from` `dana: the pricing without an earlier violation` `with the commencement` `int — the facts that fix the commencement, as the sources give them`

§§ `S02. The fee is updated on 1 January 2026 (groups 2, 4, 8)`

-- Regulation 3(a): 284 times 101.25 over 100 is 287.55, rounded to the nearest whole shekel: 288.
`dana: the application of 1 February 2026` MEANS `fixture: an application by` `dana: the applicant` `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2026 2 1)
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant with the readings on` `dana: the application of 1 February 2026` `with the amount paid being` 288 `and the readings being` `fixture: the index readings for the fees`)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant with the readings on` `dana: the application of 1 February 2026` `with the amount paid being` 284 `and the readings being` `fixture: the index readings for the fees`)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant with the readings on` `dana: the application of 1 February 2026` `with the amount paid being` 287 `and the readings being` `fixture: the index readings for the fees`)
-- Without a reading of the index the update cannot be computed: a refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant with the readings on` `dana: the application of 1 February 2026` `with the amount paid being` 288 `and the readings being` EMPTY)

§§ `S03. A foreign degree and the Council (groups 4, 2, 8)`

`noa: the application of 1 December 2025` MEANS `fixture: an application by` (`fixture: an applicant with no prior training, being` `fixture: Noa, an individual`) `for a` `grade 1 licence` `on` (YMD 2025 12 1)
-- Six of the eleven present, the chair among them: a quorum (s.25(a)); 3 against 2 carries (s.25(b)): the advice is valid, the degree recognised.
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant on a foreign degree on` `noa: the application of 1 December 2025` `after the consultation` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`)
-- Five present: no quorum, the advice is not the Council's, so the degree was not recognised and nothing else supplies the training.
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant on a foreign degree on` `noa: the application of 1 December 2025` `after the consultation` `fixture: a consultation on an individual matter at a meeting without a quorum`)
-- The Council was never asked.
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant on a foreign degree on` `noa: the application of 1 December 2025` `after the consultation` `int — a consultation that was never requested`)
-- A subcommittee's advice on an individual application (function (3)) with the Council's procedure unknown: the text does not answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant on a foreign degree on` `noa: the application of 1 December 2025` `after the consultation` (`fixture: a consultation on an individual matter advised by a subcommittee, the procedure being` NOTHING))
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant on a foreign degree on` `noa: the application of 1 December 2025` `after the consultation` (`fixture: a consultation on an individual matter advised by a subcommittee, the procedure being` (JUST TRUE)))
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar must grant the licence on` (`fixture: a grant on a foreign degree on` `noa: the application of 1 December 2025` `after the consultation` (`fixture: a consultation on an individual matter advised by a subcommittee, the procedure being` (JUST FALSE)))

§§ `S04. Hans, a foreign expert (groups 2, 8, 7, 1, 6)`

`hans: the application of 1 December 2025` MEANS `Application` WITH
    `the applicant` IS `fixture: an applicant with no prior training, being` `fixture: Hans, an individual and a foreign expert`
    `the kind of licence sought` IS `grade 3 licence`
    `an application to renew` IS FALSE
    `an application for a temporary licence` IS TRUE
    `the day of the application` IS YMD 2025 12 1
`hans: the work abroad on 1 September 2022` MEANS `Work done abroad by a foreign expert under section 9` WITH
    `the work` IS `Work item` WITH
        `performed by` IS `fixture: Hans, an individual and a foreign expert`
        `the kind of job` IS `an installation job`
        `the system` IS `fixture: a system of` 120 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a"
        `date performed` IS YMD 2022 9 1
    `on a system similar to the systems the expert was invited to work on` IS TRUE
`hans: the expert's application` MEANS `Foreign expert's application under section 9` WITH
    `the application` IS `hans: the application of 1 December 2025`
    `the applicant comes from a foreign state` IS TRUE
    `the system the expert was invited to work on` IS `fixture: a system of` 100 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a"
    `authorised to do such work in a foreign state` IS TRUE
    `work done abroad` IS LIST `hans: the work abroad on 1 September 2022`
GIVEN paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Facts of a grant of a temporary licence under section 9`
`hans: the grant facts with the amount paid being` paid MEANS `Facts of a grant of a temporary licence under section 9` WITH
    `the expert` IS `hans: the expert's application`
    `in the Registrar's opinion the expert is of repute and a renowned expert in the field` IS TRUE
    `the vintage of the Fees Regulations` IS `the Fees Regulations as made`
    `the amount paid for the application` IS paid
    `the index readings` IS EMPTY
-- Regulation 2(d) as made: 398 for the application.  Paid 398: the Registrar may grant; 397: barred.
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar may grant a temporary licence on` (`hans: the grant facts with the amount paid being` 398)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar may grant a temporary licence on` (`hans: the grant facts with the amount paid being` 397)
-- A term of one year from 1.12.2025 ends on 1.12.2026 (IL s.10(b)).
#ASSERT `s 9(a) — the latest last day of a temporary licence granted on` (YMD 2025 12 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 12 1
`hans: the temporary licence` MEANS `fixture: a temporary licence held by` `fixture: Hans, an individual and a foreign expert` `granted on` (YMD 2025 12 1) `and recorded to end on` (YMD 2026 12 1)
#ASSERT `int — the licence kinds in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 1) (LIST `hans: the temporary licence`) EQUALS LIST `grade 3 licence`
#ASSERT `int — the licence kinds in force on the day` (YMD 2026 12 1) (LIST `hans: the temporary licence`) EQUALS LIST `grade 3 licence`
#ASSERT `int — the licence kinds in force on the day` (YMD 2026 12 2) (LIST `hans: the temporary licence`) EQUALS EMPTY
-- R134a is paragraph (2): commenced 16.1.2027.  On 1.6.2026 and 2.12.2026 section 3(a) does not apply; on 20.1.2027, with the licence lapsed, it forbids.
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      system IS A `Cooling system`
GIVETH A `Situation of one piece of work`
`hans: the work on` day `of the system` system MEANS `fixture: the work of` `fixture: Hans, an individual and a foreign expert` `holding` (LIST `hans: the temporary licence`) `on` day `on the system` system `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`
`hans: the 100 kW R134a system` MEANS `fixture: a system of` 100 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a"
`hans: the 100 kW propane system` MEANS `fixture: a system of` 100 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "290"
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW R134a system`) EQUALS `section 3(a) does not apply: the Law has not yet commenced for work on the system`
#ASSERT `int — the person may do the work of` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW R134a system`)
#ASSERT `int — the person may do the work of` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2026 12 2) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW R134a system`)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the person may do the work of` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2027 1 20) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW R134a system`)
#ASSERT `int — the violation committed under section 3(a) by` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2027 1 20) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW R134a system`) `with the reference` "hans-2027-01-20" EQUALS JUST (Violation WITH `the violator` IS `fixture: Hans, an individual and a foreign expert`, `the listed violation` IS `work with no licence at all`, `reference for the act` IS "hans-2027-01-20", `date of the act` IS YMD 2027 1 20)
#ASSERT `int — the violation committed under section 3(a) by` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW R134a system`) `with the reference` "hans-2026-06-01" EQUALS NOTHING
-- Sanction on 20.1.2027: Chapter 6 (hypothetical regulation under s.46) in force from 16.1.2027; item (1) 20,000 times 102/100 = 20,400; no update since (102/102).
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for the work of` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2027 1 20) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW R134a system`) `with the reference` "hans-2027-01-20" `priced from` (`fixture: the pricing of a violation that did not continue and has no earlier violation, updated on` (YMD 2027 2 15)) `with the commencement` `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` EQUALS `the sanction is` 20400
-- Propane is paragraph (1): commenced 16.7.2025.  On 1.6.2026 the licence is in force: permitted.  On 2.12.2026 it has lapsed: forbidden, item (1); but Chapter 6 is not in force before 16.1.2027.
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW propane system`) EQUALS `the work is permitted: the person holds a licence of the kind appropriate to the system and the work, and works within its conditions`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the person may do the work of` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2026 12 2) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW propane system`)
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for the work of` (`hans: the work on` (YMD 2026 12 2) `of the system` `hans: the 100 kW propane system`) `with the reference` "hans-2026-12-02" `priced from` (`fixture: the pricing of a violation that did not continue and has no earlier violation, updated on` (YMD 2027 2 15)) `with the commencement` `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` EQUALS `no sanction: Chapter 6 had not commenced on the day of the act`

§§ `S09. Revocation under section 10(a) (groups 1, 4, 2, 7, 6)`

`dana: the licence granted on 1 February 2026` MEANS `fixture: an ordinary licence held by` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `of kind` `grade 1 licence` `granted on` (YMD 2026 2 1)
GIVEN consultation IS A `Consultation of the Council`
GIVETH A `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)`
`dana: the proposal to revoke after` consultation MEANS `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)` WITH
    `the measure` IS `revoke the licence`
    `the grounds` IS `Grounds under section 10(a)` WITH
        `the licence was granted on false, mistaken, misleading or partial information` IS FALSE
        `a condition for the grant ceased to hold` IS FALSE
        `the only condition that ceased to hold is a condition of section 6(a)(4)` IS FALSE
        `the licensee breached a licence condition` IS TRUE
        `the licensee breached a duty or prohibition under the Law or another enactment in connection with the activity as a licensee` IS FALSE
        `the licensee gave false, misleading, mistaken or partial information when it was demanded` IS FALSE
        `the licensee showed lack of professionalism or negligence that may endanger life or damage property` IS FALSE
    `the consultation of the Council` IS consultation
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE
    `the period of the restriction or suspension` IS NOTHING
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a) on` (`dana: the proposal to revoke after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a) on` (`dana: the proposal to revoke after` `fixture: a consultation on an individual matter at a meeting without a quorum`)
#ASSERT `int — the preconditions of section 10(a) not met on` (`dana: the proposal to revoke after` `fixture: a consultation on an individual matter at a meeting without a quorum`) EQUALS LIST `the Council's advice was not validly given under section 10`
#ASSERT `int — the preconditions of section 10(a) not met on` (`dana: the proposal to revoke after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a) on` (`dana: the proposal to revoke after` (`fixture: a consultation on an individual matter advised by a subcommittee, the procedure being` (JUST TRUE)))
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a) on` (`dana: the proposal to revoke after` (`fixture: a consultation on an individual matter advised by a subcommittee, the procedure being` NOTHING))
-- The register records the revocation on 1.5.2028: in force on 30.4.2028, not on 1.5.2028 (group 1 fork F27 and group 2 fork FV6 agree).
`dana: the licence revoked on 1 May 2028` MEANS `fixture: the licence` `dana: the licence granted on 1 February 2026` `after the register records it revoked on` (YMD 2028 5 1)
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence revoked on 1 May 2028` (YMD 2028 4 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence revoked on 1 May 2028` (YMD 2028 5 1)
#ASSERT `s 10 — the licence is revoked on the day` `dana: the licence revoked on 1 May 2028` (YMD 2028 5 1)
#ASSERT NOT `s 10 — the licence is revoked on the day` `dana: the licence revoked on 1 May 2028` (YMD 2028 4 30)
`dana: the work on 1 May 2028` MEANS `fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST `dana: the licence revoked on 1 May 2028`) `on` (YMD 2028 5 1) `on the system` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` `dana: the work on 1 May 2028` EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for the work of` `dana: the work on 1 May 2028` `with the reference` "dana-2028-05-01" `priced from` (`fixture: the pricing of a violation that did not continue and has no earlier violation, updated on` (YMD 2028 6 20)) `with the commencement` `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` EQUALS `the sanction is` 20400

§§ `S16. Suspension until final judgment (groups 1, 4, 2, 6)`

`dana: the facts of the suspension after` MEANS `Facts of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS TRUE
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS TRUE
    `the consultation of the Council` IS `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment on` `dana: the facts of the suspension after`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment on` (`Facts of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS TRUE, `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS TRUE, `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS TRUE, `the consultation of the Council` IS `fixture: a consultation on an individual matter at a meeting without a quorum`, `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE)
`dana: the licence suspended from 1 March 2028 without end` MEANS `fixture: the licence` `dana: the licence granted on 1 February 2026` `after the register records it suspended from` (YMD 2028 3 1) `until` NOTHING
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence suspended from 1 March 2028 without end` (YMD 2028 2 29)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence suspended from 1 March 2028 without end` (YMD 2028 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence suspended from 1 March 2028 without end` (YMD 2030 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 10 — the licence is suspended on the day` `dana: the licence suspended from 1 March 2028 without end` (YMD 2030 1 1)
`dana: the work on 1 March 2028` MEANS `fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST `dana: the licence suspended from 1 March 2028 without end`) `on` (YMD 2028 3 1) `on the system` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` `dana: the work on 1 March 2028` EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`
-- The judgment on 10.6.2029: "until" includes the day (IL s.8), so the suspension ends on that day; group 1's own function and group 2's register agree.
`dana: the licence suspended from 1 March 2028 until 10 June 2029` MEANS `fixture: the licence` `dana: the licence granted on 1 February 2026` `after the register records it suspended from` (YMD 2028 3 1) `until` (JUST (YMD 2029 6 10))
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence suspended from 1 March 2028 until 10 June 2029` (YMD 2029 6 10)
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence suspended from 1 March 2028 until 10 June 2029` (YMD 2029 6 11)
#ASSERT `a suspension under section 10(b) is in force on the day` (YMD 2028 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2029 6 10)) (YMD 2029 6 10)
#ASSERT NOT `a suspension under section 10(b) is in force on the day` (YMD 2028 3 1) (JUST (YMD 2029 6 10)) (YMD 2029 6 11)
#ASSERT `a suspension under section 10(b) is in force on the day` (YMD 2028 3 1) NOTHING (YMD 2035 1 1)

§§ `S10. The training duty as a condition of the licence (groups 3, 4, 2, 1, 6)`

-- Dana, licence granted 1.2.2026 (in force to 1.2.2031).  The Registrar requires a course on 10.6.2027 (notice 1.5.2027, Council valid).  She does not attend.
GIVEN consultation IS A `Consultation of the Council`
      attended IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Requirement of a particular course under section 17(b)`
`dana: the requirement to attend the course of 10 June 2027 after` consultation `and the attendance being` attended MEANS `Requirement of a particular course under section 17(b)` WITH
    `the day of the course` IS YMD 2027 6 10
    `the day notice of the requirement was given` IS YMD 2027 5 1
    `the course was conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Training Division` IS TRUE
    `the consultation of the Council about requiring the course` IS consultation
    `in the Registrar's opinion circumstances justify requiring attendance` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion attendance is required to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law` IS TRUE
    `notice was given a reasonable time before the date of the course` IS TRUE
    `the licensee attended the course` IS attended
    `the licensee met the requirements of the course` IS attended
GIVEN consultation IS A `Consultation of the Council`
      attended IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Training record under one licence`
`dana: the training records for the course after` consultation `and the attendance being` attended MEANS
    LIST `Training record under one licence` WITH
        `the licence the record concerns` IS `dana: the licence granted on 1 February 2026`
        `the sessions attended` IS EMPTY
        `the courses required under section 17(b)` IS LIST `int — the course required under section 17(b) by` (`dana: the requirement to attend the course of 10 June 2027 after` consultation `and the attendance being` attended)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      records IS A LIST OF `Training record under one licence`
GIVETH A `Situation of one piece of work`
`dana: the work on` day `with the training records` records MEANS `fixture: training records added to the situation` (`fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST `dana: the licence granted on 1 February 2026`) `on` day `on the system` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`) `being` records
-- On 9.6.2027 the day of the course has not passed: no breach, work permitted.
#ASSERT `int — the person may do the work of` (`dana: the work on` (YMD 2027 6 9) `with the training records` (`dana: the training records for the course after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter` `and the attendance being` FALSE))
-- On 11.6.2027 she has not attended: the condition of s.17(d) is breached, so s.3(a) forbids although she holds a licence of the right kind.
#ASSERT `int — a licence condition was breached in the situation` (`dana: the work on` (YMD 2027 6 11) `with the training records` (`dana: the training records for the course after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter` `and the attendance being` FALSE))
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` (`dana: the work on` (YMD 2027 6 11) `with the training records` (`dana: the training records for the course after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter` `and the attendance being` FALSE)) EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds a licence of the appropriate kind but works outside its conditions or the provisions under the Law`
-- No Third Schedule item prices a breach of a condition (trap T12): no listed violation, so no sanction row.
#ASSERT `int — the violation committed under section 3(a) by` (`dana: the work on` (YMD 2027 6 11) `with the training records` (`dana: the training records for the course after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter` `and the attendance being` FALSE)) `with the reference` "dana-2027-06-11" EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `int — the sanction for the work of` (`dana: the work on` (YMD 2027 6 11) `with the training records` (`dana: the training records for the course after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter` `and the attendance being` FALSE)) `with the reference` "dana-2027-06-11" `priced from` (`fixture: the pricing of a violation that did not continue and has no earlier violation, updated on` (YMD 2027 8 1)) `with the commencement` `fixture: the commencement facts with a hypothetical regulation under section 46` EQUALS `no listed violation: the facts breach no provision that the Third Schedule prices`
-- She attended and met the requirements: permitted.
#ASSERT `int — the person may do the work of` (`dana: the work on` (YMD 2027 6 11) `with the training records` (`dana: the training records for the course after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter` `and the attendance being` TRUE))
-- The Council's advice was not validly given (five present): the requirement was not lawfully made, so there is no duty to attend and no breach.
#ASSERT `int — the person may do the work of` (`dana: the work on` (YMD 2027 6 11) `with the training records` (`dana: the training records for the course after` `fixture: a consultation on an individual matter at a meeting without a quorum` `and the attendance being` FALSE))

§§ `S11. An extension of validity under section 17(c), across 31 March (groups 3, 4, 2, 1)`

-- Dana's licence granted 1.6.2025: five years would end 1.6.2030, 31 March of the fifth year from the year of grant is 31.3.2030: the earlier is 31.3.2030.
`dana: the licence granted on 1 June 2025` MEANS `fixture: an ordinary licence held by` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `of kind` `grade 1 licence` `granted on` (YMD 2025 6 1)
#ASSERT `s 8 — the last day of validity of the licence` `dana: the licence granted on 1 June 2025` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 31
GIVEN consultation IS A `Consultation of the Council`
GIVETH A `Decision to extend the validity of a licence`
`dana: the decision of 15 March 2030 to extend to 30 June 2030 after` consultation MEANS `Decision to extend the validity of a licence` WITH
    `the day of the Registrar's decision` IS YMD 2030 3 15
    `the last day of validity fixed by the extension` IS YMD 2030 6 30
    `the licensee had not fulfilled the duty under section 17(a) or (b)` IS TRUE
    `the consultation of the Council about the extension` IS consultation
    `in the Registrar's opinion these are special cases and the circumstances are justified` IS TRUE
    `the extension is granted so that the licensee can fulfil the duty` IS TRUE
-- Three months after 31.3.2030 is 30.6.2030 (IL s.10(b)); group 2's helper and group 3's agree.
#ASSERT `s 17(c) — the last day of validity` (YMD 2030 3 31) `extended by` 3 `months` EQUALS YMD 2030 6 30
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence by the decision` `dana: the licence granted on 1 June 2025` (`dana: the decision of 15 March 2030 to extend to 30 June 2030 after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence by the decision` `dana: the licence granted on 1 June 2025` (`dana: the decision of 15 March 2030 to extend to 30 June 2030 after` `fixture: a consultation on an individual matter at a meeting without a quorum`) TRUE
`dana: the licence extended to 30 June 2030` MEANS `int — the licence after the decision to extend` `dana: the licence granted on 1 June 2025` (`dana: the decision of 15 March 2030 to extend to 30 June 2030 after` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`) TRUE
`dana: the licence after a refused extension` MEANS `int — the licence after the decision to extend` `dana: the licence granted on 1 June 2025` (`dana: the decision of 15 March 2030 to extend to 30 June 2030 after` `fixture: a consultation on an individual matter at a meeting without a quorum`) TRUE
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence extended to 30 June 2030` (YMD 2030 4 1)
#ASSERT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence extended to 30 June 2030` (YMD 2030 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence extended to 30 June 2030` (YMD 2030 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the licence is in force on` `dana: the licence after a refused extension` (YMD 2030 4 1)
-- Work on 1.4.2030: permitted with the extension (no training sessions, but the window closes on the extended last day); forbidden without it (item (1)).
GIVEN licence IS A Licence
GIVETH A `Situation of one piece of work`
`dana: the work on 1 April 2030 holding` licence MEANS `fixture: training records added to the situation` (`fixture: the work of` `fixture: Dana, an individual` `holding` (LIST licence) `on` (YMD 2030 4 1) `on the system` (`fixture: a system of` 10 `kilowatts using refrigerant` "134a") `amounting to` `A.1(2) connecting piping and conductors to the units`) `being` (LIST `Training record under one licence` WITH `the licence the record concerns` IS licence, `the sessions attended` IS EMPTY, `the courses required under section 17(b)` IS EMPTY)
#ASSERT `int — the person may do the work of` (`dana: the work on 1 April 2030 holding` `dana: the licence extended to 30 June 2030`)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the person may do the work of` (`dana: the work on 1 April 2030 holding` `dana: the licence granted on 1 June 2025`)
#ASSERT `int — the outcome of section 3(a) for the work of` (`dana: the work on 1 April 2030 holding` `dana: the licence granted on 1 June 2025`) EQUALS `the work is forbidden: the person holds no licence at all`
#ASSERT NOT `int — the person may do the work of` (`dana: the work on 1 April 2030 holding` `dana: the licence after a refused extension`)

§§ `S19. A condition for the grant ceased to hold: ground (2) of section 10(a) (groups 2, 1, 4)`

-- Dana is later convicted of a criminal offence that the Registrar finds disqualifying.  Group 2 re-examines s.6(a)(1) to (3) for an ordinary licence (the training of (4) is not re-asked); the negation is ground (2) of s.10(a) (IP18).
`dana: the record after a criminal conviction` MEANS `Record of offences` WITH
    `convicted of a criminal offence` IS TRUE
    `convicted of a disciplinary offence` IS FALSE
    `charged with a criminal offence and no final judgment yet` IS FALSE
    `a disciplinary complaint is pending with no final judgment` IS FALSE
`dana: the applicant after a criminal conviction` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `the person` IS `fixture: Dana, an individual`
    `of full age` IS TRUE
    `an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
    `an Israeli resident` IS TRUE
    `record of offences` IS `dana: the record after a criminal conviction`
    `licences held` IS LIST `dana: the licence granted on 1 February 2026`
    `certificates held` IS EMPTY
    `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
    `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
    `completed a study programme that includes the complement course` IS FALSE
    `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch` IS FALSE
    `periods of work on cooling systems` IS EMPTY
    `holds a valid electrician licence of a kind listed in the Electricity Regulations` IS FALSE
    `holds a valid working-at-height approval` IS FALSE
`dana: the renewal application of 1 February 2031` MEANS Application WITH
    `the applicant` IS `dana: the applicant after a criminal conviction`
    `the kind of licence sought` IS `grade 1 licence`
    `an application to renew` IS TRUE
    `an application for a temporary licence` IS FALSE
    `the day of the application` IS YMD 2031 1 31
GIVEN opinion IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`dana: a condition for the grant ceased to hold, the Registrar's opinion of the offence being` opinion MEANS
    `int — a condition for the grant of the licence ceased to hold` `dana: the licence granted on 1 February 2026` (`the conditions of a licence under section 6 still hold` `dana: the renewal application of 1 February 2031` opinion) TRUE
#ASSERT `dana: a condition for the grant ceased to hold, the Registrar's opinion of the offence being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `dana: a condition for the grant ceased to hold, the Registrar's opinion of the offence being` FALSE
GIVEN ground2 IS A BOOLEAN
      consultation IS A `Consultation of the Council`
GIVETH A `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)`
`dana: the proposal to revoke on ground (2) alone, the ground being` ground2 `and the advice` consultation MEANS `Facts of a measure under section 10(a)` WITH
    `the measure` IS `revoke the licence`
    `the grounds` IS `Grounds under section 10(a)` WITH
        `the licence was granted on false, mistaken, misleading or partial information` IS FALSE
        `a condition for the grant ceased to hold` IS ground2
        `the only condition that ceased to hold is a condition of section 6(a)(4)` IS FALSE
        `the licensee breached a licence condition` IS FALSE
        `the licensee breached a duty or prohibition under the Law or another enactment in connection with the activity as a licensee` IS FALSE
        `the licensee gave false, misleading, mistaken or partial information when it was demanded` IS FALSE
        `the licensee showed lack of professionalism or negligence that may endanger life or damage property` IS FALSE
    `the consultation of the Council` IS consultation
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE
    `the period of the restriction or suspension` IS NOTHING
-- With the offence found disqualifying, ground (2) is made out and, after a valid consultation, the Registrar may revoke; with the opinion the other way the conditions still hold, no ground is made out, and he may not.
#ASSERT `int — the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a) on` (`dana: the proposal to revoke on ground (2) alone, the ground being` (`dana: a condition for the grant ceased to hold, the Registrar's opinion of the offence being` TRUE) `and the advice` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a) on` (`dana: the proposal to revoke on ground (2) alone, the ground being` (`dana: a condition for the grant ceased to hold, the Registrar's opinion of the offence being` FALSE) `and the advice` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`)
#ASSERT `int — the preconditions of section 10(a) not met on` (`dana: the proposal to revoke on ground (2) alone, the ground being` (`dana: a condition for the grant ceased to hold, the Registrar's opinion of the offence being` FALSE) `and the advice` `fixture: a valid consultation on an individual matter`) EQUALS LIST `no ground of section 10(a) is made out`

§§ `S20. Renewal under section 8 (groups 2, 8, 7)`

-- Renewal asks s.6(a)(1) to (3) and not the training of (4); regulation 4 still asks the fee (288 on 1.10.2026: 284 times 101.25/100); and the application must be made on or after the commencement day.
GIVEN applicant IS AN Applicant
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH AN Application
`a renewal application by` applicant `made on` day MEANS Application WITH
    `the applicant` IS applicant
    `the kind of licence sought` IS `grade 1 licence`
    `an application to renew` IS TRUE
    `an application for a temporary licence` IS FALSE
    `the day of the application` IS day
GIVEN application IS AN Application
      opinion IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Facts of a renewal under section 8`
`the renewal facts of` application `with the opinion` opinion `and the amount paid` paid MEANS `Facts of a renewal under section 8` WITH
    `the application` IS application
    `in the Registrar's opinion an offence the applicant was convicted of or is charged with makes the applicant unfit to be a licensee` IS opinion
    `the vintage of the Fees Regulations` IS `the Fees Regulations as made`
    `the amount paid for the renewal` IS paid
    `the index readings` IS `fixture: the index readings for the fees`
#ASSERT `int — the licence can be renewed on` (`the renewal facts of` (`a renewal application by` `dana: the applicant` `made on` (YMD 2026 10 1)) `with the opinion` FALSE `and the amount paid` 288)
#ASSERT NOT `int — the licence can be renewed on` (`the renewal facts of` (`a renewal application by` `dana: the applicant` `made on` (YMD 2026 10 1)) `with the opinion` FALSE `and the amount paid` 284)
-- A conviction the Registrar finds disqualifying defeats the renewal although the fee is paid; if he finds it does not disqualify, the renewal can proceed.
#ASSERT NOT `int — the licence can be renewed on` (`the renewal facts of` (`a renewal application by` `dana: the applicant after a criminal conviction` `made on` (YMD 2026 10 1)) `with the opinion` TRUE `and the amount paid` 288)
#ASSERT `int — the licence can be renewed on` (`the renewal facts of` (`a renewal application by` `dana: the applicant after a criminal conviction` `made on` (YMD 2026 10 1)) `with the opinion` FALSE `and the amount paid` 288)
-- Before the commencement day: the sources do not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED `int — the licence can be renewed on` (`the renewal facts of` (`a renewal application by` `dana: the applicant` `made on` (YMD 2025 7 15)) `with the opinion` FALSE `and the amount paid` 284)

§§ `S22. A graded certificate is the way through item 1 (groups 2, 1)`

-- Written from the Hebrew text before it was run.  Second Schedule Part B, item 1: "no prior training or experience", training of up to 480 hours conferring a final certificate of grade 2, or the Ministry of Education certificate.
-- An applicant who already holds the Training Division certificate of grade 2 has completed that course.
-- Taken (group 2, fork FS10, assumed, not ruled): the certificate is the way through item 1, so item 1 is the only item that applies and nothing further is asked.
-- The literal reading would put the holder in the row for "a certificate from the Training Division" (item 5, up to 50 hours more); that reading is group 2's alternative and its own tests cover it.
`S22: Dana holding the grade 2 Training Division certificate` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `the person` IS `fixture: Dana, an individual`
    `of full age` IS TRUE
    `an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
    `an Israeli resident` IS TRUE
    `record of offences` IS `dana: the record after a criminal conviction`
    `licences held` IS EMPTY
    `certificates held` IS LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`
    `registered as a certified technician in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
    `registered as a certified practical engineer in refrigeration and air conditioning` IS FALSE
    `completed a study programme that includes the complement course` IS FALSE
    `registered as an engineer in the mechanical branch` IS FALSE
    `periods of work on cooling systems` IS EMPTY
    `holds a valid electrician licence of a kind listed in the Electricity Regulations` IS FALSE
    `holds a valid working-at-height approval` IS FALSE
`S22: the application for a grade 2 licence on 1 December 2025` MEANS Application WITH
    `the applicant` IS `S22: Dana holding the grade 2 Training Division certificate`
    `the kind of licence sought` IS `grade 2 licence`
    `an application to renew` IS FALSE
    `an application for a temporary licence` IS FALSE
    `the day of the application` IS YMD 2025 12 1
`S22: the items` MEANS `int — the training the Second Schedule requires for` `S22: the application for a grade 2 licence on 1 December 2025`
#ASSERT NOT any (GIVEN item YIELD NOT (item's `the item number` EQUALS 1)) `S22: the items`
#ASSERT any (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number` EQUALS 1 AND item's `the part: the licence kind it leads to` EQUALS `grade 2 licence`) `S22: the items`
